<h2>Custom Agents</h2>

<p>
    Custom agents are smart shortcuts that automate common workflows. Think of them as helpful assistants that can perform a series of actions with just one click.
</p>

<p>
    Here's how they work:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Context-aware</strong> – Agents know what page you're on and can use that information. For example, an agent on a renewal page knows which renewal you're working with</li>
    <li><strong>Quick questions</strong> – Some agents ask a simple question before running (like "Which template should I use?") while others just go ahead and do their job</li>
    <li><strong>Workflow automation</strong> – An agent might send an email, create a task, update a status, and attach a file—all in one action</li>
    <li><strong>Available everywhere</strong> – You'll find agent buttons throughout Quickfire in places where they make sense</li>
</ul>

<p>
    For example, you might have an agent that says "Send Loss Run Request." When you click it, it knows you're working on a specific renewal, creates a task, sends a pre-written email to the carrier, and logs the activity—all automatically.
</p>

